e been inconclusive when  asked question the tulpa will respond  with unintelligible garbled responses  that when slowed down appear to be  traditional Tibetan mantras repeated  hundreds of times a second  scp-1447-1 does seem to exhibit signs of  intelligence and even deceit as on one  occasion it was observed goading  security Personnel into attacking it  with explosive devices as it was near  the entrance of another scp's enclosure  leading to a double breach event  scp-1447-2 is the designation given to  the man currently confined to his  quarters inside the containment site he  is a software and Hardware engineer and  entrepreneur whose name has been  redacted from official records we will  refer to him from Huron simply as Steve  the following is information the subject  gave SCP Foundation staff willingly  Steve was an accomplished man excelling  at everything he did and finding a great  level of success in the tech sector as a  developer and entrepreneur and yet with  all the riches and Fame that his success  brought him he found himself wanting  more his obsessiveness for a sense of  meaningful fulfillment led him to drive  away loved ones and dive further into  his work creating a vicious cycle of  self-isolation leaving him with a  greater sense of unfulfillment from his  life one day Steve came to the  realization that what he needed was to  split away from the reality he had  created for himself he needed to find  peace and he knew he couldn't do it  where he currently was he packed a bag  and without a second thought decided to  leave everything behind without saying a  word to anyone about where he was going  but where was he going he had thought to  himself following a trend of westerners  traveling to Asia to find a new sense of  Enlightenment Steve boarded the playing  to Ching Hai Province China where he had  joined an order of monastic monks as he  did with most aspects of his life he  threw himself entirety into the practice  dressing like the brothers of the order  in the traditional monastic Garb and  even electing to shave his head bare  switching to a vegetarian diet and  learning the Tibetan mantras he put his  sole effort into learning the art of  deep meditation vowing to truly split  away from the repetitive unfulfilling  life he had chosen to leave behind  during one particular lesson Steve  learned from an elder brother at the  monastery about the concept of a tulpa a  method where a person enters deep  focused meditation to conjure a physical  visual manifestation of a specific  thought or emotion being new to the  practice at the time Steve couldn't find  himself thinking of anything but the  image of a laughing Buddha he was used  to seeing every time he entered a local  Chinese restaurant back in the United  States he remembered how the image made  him feel welcome how the look of Joy on  the Buddha's face brought a look of joy  to his own explaining this to the  brothers at the monastery they promptly  corrected him that this image is not an  image of the Buddha as in the sense of  the Buddha being a single defined deity  but just one of the many interpretations  of Buddha The Laughing Buddha is  particularly a cultural symbol of luck  and abundance the monks asked Steve to  picture something else when attempting  to visualize a tulpa such as an emotion  that has taken form and shape but try as  he could Steve had become fixated on the  image of the popular laughing Buddha and  could do little to imagine anything else  on his own Steve meditated persistently  in this endeavor truly expecting success  and working towards it with a fervent  drive he put into every project in his  life and to the amazement of himself and  the brothers of the monastery his tulpa  slowly began to manifest it was small at  first only an image that he could see he  didn't think much of it not thinking  that he had created anything real he  believed the image of the Laughing  Buddha in front of him was just an  overactivation of the visual centers of  his brain most likely due to the strain  from long hours of meditation deciding  to humor his imagination he began  treating the tall but like he would any  brother of the temple speaking to it out  loud and showing it respect and  inclusion it was like having his own  imaginary friend yet over time the tulpa  began to become more than just an image  it began to have a physical effect on  objects around him a bucket kicked over  a chair pulled back as a brother went to  sit down the imaginary friend was now  more like a mischievous invisible  prankster but still only one he could  see the brothers began to grow weary of  the tulpa and with it grew weary of the  Foreigner that had brought it into  existence meanwhile Steve had become  amazed at his level of success he began  to wonder if he could manifest other  thoughts into existence he began to  think about his life his career his  level of success he began to think about  how he could apply himself to impart his  will on reality how he wanted more he  focused on this goal of meditation and  yet could not help but find frustration  in his efforts it didn't help that the  brothers of the monastery now openly  presented him Steve's demeanor began to  change and become less optimistic and  more obsessed with the memory of the  repetitive monotony of his old life  before coming to the monastery his tulpa  too began to change no longer fat with  joy its appearance began to thin what  was once an embodiment of laughter and  happiness began to morph into a darker  more mischievous entity the pranks too  became more dangerous the tulpa began  leaving buckets of scalding hot water  above door frames for unsuspecting monks  to walk through it then began filling  the sandals of monks with snakes  thankfully for the brothers of the  monastery snakes weren't poisonous until  suddenly on one particular occasion they  were a pair of fayette's vipers appeared  in the sandals of a brother of the  monastery venomous snakes that could  only be found hundreds of miles away in  the south of Tibet in a region Steve had  never heard of and had never been to it  was an impossibility for him to have  given birth to the manifestation of this  act without its requisite knowledge did  this mean the tulpa had gained some  means of self-actualization could it  contemplate its own sentience seeking to  learn more answers about the nature of  the tulpa Steve studied the teachings of  the Buddha and the quests for  enlightenment about Nirvana and the end  to the cycle of death and rebirth in his  mind Steve began to intertwine those  ideas with the memory of the mundanity  of his previous life and the feelings  that lingered in his stomach of it being  unfulfilling and empty how he had  desperately wanted the daily cycle of  mundanity to end how he wanted peace  little did he know in doing so he was  creating a manifestation with the  express goal of ending his life as Steve  began to enter longer and deeper  sessions of meditation the tulpa began  to grow more self-actualizing and  independent of his will it became harder  to control Maleficent and one day Steve  realized he could no longer picture The  Laughing Buddha that had once filled him  with joy from that moment on the toppa's  face became unrecognizable and was no  longer in a fixed state but in constant  movement so that no facial features  could be visible it was that night the  monks had caught the tulpa holding a  knife to Steve's throat channeling their  meditative power of actualization they  managed to collectively banish the tulpa  from the monastery but it was not for  long the toppa began to follow Steve  wherever he went a physical embodiment  of his wish to end the repeating cycle  of his life and bring him peace peace by  means of the extinguishing of his life  the existence of  scp-1447-1 was first brought to the  attention of foundation staff when Steve  arrived at site-73 seeking Sanctuary  from the tulpa he had been running from  it is unclear to Foundation staff how  the software Mogul came to know of the  location of site-73 all that could be  gained from questioning him on the  matter is that he received the  information from the monks at a lamisary  in qinghai Province China Steve was  given the designation  scp-1447-2 because of his relation to  the entity and then placed in Secure  confinement at the facility two days  later security Personnel made contact  with the entity when it attacked the  facility in search of the tech Mogul  resulting in the death of two agents the  attacks from scp-1447 ceased when Steve  was evacuated via airlift to London and  then later moved again to site-60 in  just three weeks after this change the  tulpa had already caught up with Steve  attacking the facility and becoming  enraged by the interference from  security Personnel slaughtering  countless members of SCP staff in its  wake it is here at this facility that  the members of security Personnel were  first able to use High Caliber Firepower  to push back the topaz Advance into a  makeshift concrete enclosure which would  eventually come to be  scp-1447-1's current attainment cell Dr  rolfus an SCP researcher was the first  to interview Steve after assigning him  to the designation  scp-1447-2 he was given this designation  when Foundation staff realized that the  person known as Steve real name redacted  had in fact never left the United States  for Ching Hai Province and had been  leading his life as a successful Tech  Mogul without any notable Interruption  researchers became unsure whether Steve  was in fact who he said he was or  instead an entity similar to  scp-1447-1 when confronted with images  of his doppelganger in news and media  reports living out his life and assuming  his identity  scp-1447-2 was unable to explain the  anomaly and asserted that he was the  true original version of himself  suggesting that a rival technology  company or even his own 